  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 371fcced5420eda46b9cb39fda4431ce, type: 3}
  m_Name: Rose
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::FlowerData
  id: rose
  displayName: Rose
  scientificName: "Rosa \xD7 hybrida"
  markerImageName: rose
  description: The rose is a flowering shrub admired for its layered petals, elegant
    shape and wide range of colours. Garden roses have been developed through centuries
    of cultivation and hybridisation. Their flowers may be single or densely petalled,
    and many varieties have a strong, sweet fragrance. Roses are widely grown in
    gardens and are among the most popular flowers used in bouquets.
  origin: Cultivated hybrids developed from rose species native mainly to Europe,
    Asia, North America and North Africa
  meaning: 'Love, beauty and affection. Red roses represent romantic love, pink roses
    represent admiration and gratitude, white roses represent purity and remembrance,
    yellow roses represent friendship and joy, and orange roses represent enthusiasm
    and desire. '
  habitat: Gardens, parks, hedges and open sunny areas with fertile, moisture-retentive
    but well-drained soil.
  birthflower: June
  floweringSeason: 'Late spring to autumn, usually from May to October, depending
    on the variety and climate '
  sunlight: 'Full sun is best. Provide at least six hours of direct sunlight each
    day. Some varieties can tolerate partial shade, but they may produce fewer flowers. '
  watering: 'Water deeply when the upper layer of soil begins to dry. Direct the
    water toward the base of the plant and avoid regularly wetting the leaves. Keep
    the soil evenly moist, especially during hot weather, but do not allow it to
    become waterlogged. '
  difficulty: Moderate
  arScale: 0.05
  flowerImage: {fileID: 0}
